# The build context was 6.1 GB, of which `venv/` alone is 6.0 GB — sent to the daemon
# on every single build, for a Dockerfile that copies about 1 MB of it.
#
# This is an **allow-list**: everything is excluded, then the paths the Dockerfile
# actually COPYs are added back. A deny-list goes stale — it would have to be edited
# every time the repo grows a directory — while this one cannot let anything in by
# accident. The cost is that adding a `COPY` to the Dockerfile means adding its source
# here too, and forgetting fails the build loudly ("file not found") rather than
# quietly shipping the wrong thing.
*

!requirements.txt
!alembic.ini
!alembic
!app
!job_qa_service
!scripts
!Merged_Occupations.xlsx

# …minus the noise that lives inside those directories.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
